For growth $y=a^{x}$ with $a>1$: as $x\to\infty$, $y\to\infty$; as $x\to-\infty$, $y\to0$ from above.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty, xmin=-3.4, xmax=2.4, ymin=-1, ymax=4.6, samples=100, clip=false, width=9cm, height=7.5cm]
\addplot[dashed, domain=-3.2:2.2] (x, 0);
\addplot[thick, <->, smooth, domain=-3.2:1.54] {exp(0.9*x)} node[pos=0.92, left, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$y=a^{x}$};
\node[below] at (axis cs:-2.4,0) {$y=0$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Decay $y=a^{-x}$ with $a>1$ reverses this: as $x\to\infty$, $y\to0$; as $x\to-\infty$, $y\to\infty$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty, xmin=-2.4, xmax=3.4, ymin=-1, ymax=4.6, samples=100, clip=false, width=9cm, height=7.5cm]
\addplot[dashed, domain=-2.2:3.2] (x, 0);
\addplot[thick, <->, smooth, domain=-1.54:3.2] {exp(-0.9*x)} node[pos=0.75, above right, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$y=a^{-x}$};
\node[below] at (axis cs:2.4,0) {$y=0$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A vertical shift $y=k(a^{x})+c$ moves the asymptote to $y=c$, so the approaching end tends to $c$ instead of $0$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty, xmin=-3.4, xmax=3.2, ymin=-1.4, ymax=4.8, samples=100, clip=false, width=9cm, height=7.5cm]
\addplot[dashed, domain=-3.2:3.0] (x, 1.6);
\addplot[thick, <->, smooth, domain=-3.2:1.293] {1.6+exp(0.9*x)} node[pos=0.9, right, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$y=k(a^{x})+c$};
\node[above] at (axis cs:2.5,1.6) {$y=c$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A negative $k$ flips the curve vertically, so the growing end tends to $-\infty$ and the asymptote is approached from below.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty, xmin=-3.4, xmax=3.0, ymin=-4.6, ymax=1.0, samples=100, clip=false, width=9cm, height=7.5cm]
\addplot[dashed, domain=-3.2:2.8] (x, 0);
\addplot[thick, <->, smooth, domain=-3.2:1.54] {-exp(0.9*x)} node[pos=0.85, right, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$y=k(a^{x})$};
\node[above] at (axis cs:-2.4,0) {$y=0$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
The base $4>1$, so the exponential increases as $x$ increases.

As $x\to\infty$, $4^x\to\infty$, so $y\to\infty$.

As $x\to-\infty$, $4^x\to0$ from above, so $y\to0$.

Horizontal asymptote: $y=0$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=5.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},tick label style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},xtick=\empty,ytick=\empty,xmin=-2.5,xmax=1.5,ymin=-0.8,ymax=5,samples=100,clip=false]
\addplot[black,thick,<->,domain=-2.3:1.08] {4^x};
\node[font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black,anchor=west] at (axis cs:0.4,2.5) {$y=4^x$};
\node[font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black,anchor=north] at (axis cs:-1.5,0) {$y=0$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

First identify the behaviour of the exponential term. Its coefficient determines the direction of the unbounded end; the added constant gives the horizontal asymptote.

(a) As $x\to\infty$, $4^x\to\infty$, so $y\to\infty$. As $x\to-\infty$, $4^x\to0$, so $y\to-3$ from above. Asymptote: $y=-3$.

(b) As $x\to\infty$, $5^x\to\infty$, so $y\to-\infty$. As $x\to-\infty$, $5^x\to0$, so $y\to6$ from below. Asymptote: $y=6$.

(c) As $x\to\infty$, $4^{-x}\to0$, so $y\to-2$ from above. As $x\to-\infty$, $4^{-x}\to\infty$, so $y\to\infty$. Asymptote: $y=-2$.

(d) As $x\to\infty$, $5^{-x}\to0$, so $y\to4$ from below. As $x\to-\infty$, $5^{-x}\to\infty$, so $y\to-\infty$. Asymptote: $y=4$.

The sketch shows part (d).

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=5.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},tick label style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},xtick=\empty,ytick=\empty,xmin=-1.4,xmax=3,ymin=-4,ymax=5.5,samples=100,clip=false]
\addplot[black,dashed,domain=-1.2:2.8] {4};
\addplot[black,thick,<->,domain=-0.82:2.8] {4-2*5^(-x)};
\node[font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black,anchor=south] at (axis cs:2,4) {$y=4$};
\node[font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black,anchor=west] at (axis cs:0.2,1.8) {$y=4-2(5^{-x})$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
